{
  "schema": "trawf_archetype_catalog_v4",
  "source": "design_archetypes.md",
  "notes": "Each archetype has a STAGE (campaign introduction order, 1=earliest). Approaches carry min_stage: a primary/basic-shadow approach is in-stage; a 'shadow_expert' approach borrows a later-stage technique (min_stage > stage) and is the Layer-3 mastery move Aster+Peris use on a second/expert playthrough (per design_principles_shadow_solutions.md). The solver gates the full party (spotlight) to min_stage<=progression_stage but lets the Aster+Peris shadow use any stage; every archetype still keeps a bare-pair shadow approach so the pair can ALWAYS finish. SURVIVAL archetypes (12-16, kind 'survival') carry survival metadata: survival_kind (forage|exploit|gauntlet|hazard|rest), atp_reward (pips banked at a forage cache, GDD 2.4), pressure_cost (HP/stamina attrition at a gauntlet/hazard), exploit_target (an enemy-vs-enemy pairing the party can weaponise). They keep the same primary(specialist)/shadow(aster_peris) approach split so they stay multi-solution, bare-pair solvable, and stage-gated.",
